Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: handle H264 stream-mode data requests

SC2 H264 MULTI runs in stream mode over a continuous VIFIFO, but gives
firmware a finite input bit budget on each run. The producer may advance
WP before that budget is exhausted. Firmware then requests more data with
status 0x12 even though another committed packet is already available.

A powered live-TV capture showed mode 2, a 3232-byte job with zero bits
remaining, no current picture and no decoder error, while the committed
end had already advanced to byte 4485. Treating this as an unknown fatal
mailbox aborted both vb2 queues.

Match the BSP stream-mode protocol: DATA_REQUEST enters the same empty
handling as SEARCH_BUFEMPTY and DECODE_BUFEMPTY. This is not the disabled
frame-mode GET_DATA handoff between noncontiguous chunks. Preserve the
last completed-picture checkpoint and token ledger, release only an
unfinished picture's own resources, and restart only when new input has
been committed. Never turn the request into picture completion.

At drain, allow a terminal data request only with the existing complete
picture/field and empty-token checks. Incomplete pictures or unmatched
fields still fail rather than manufacturing output or successful EOS.

Requires the native H264 MULTI and drain integration through 0070/0071.
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
@@ -5085,4 +5085,10 @@
         break;
     }
+    /* Stream mode can exhaust its bit budget while the producer advances WP.
+     * DATA_REQUEST is starvation, not a completed picture or a frame-based
+     * chunk handoff. Keep the last completed input checkpoint and all tokens;
+     * replay unfinished input only after more bytes have been committed.
+     */
+    case H264_DATA_REQUEST:
     case H264_SEARCH_BUFEMPTY:
     case H264_DECODE_BUFEMPTY: {
@@ -5222,7 +5228,9 @@
-    /* SEARCH_BUFEMPTY plus the completed-picture ledger is real drain.
+    /* Search starvation plus the completed-picture ledger is real drain.
      * No timeout, cached ANC surface, or missing field becomes a picture.
      */
-    if (m->incomplete || m->empty_status != H264_SEARCH_BUFEMPTY) {
+    if (m->incomplete ||
+        (m->empty_status != H264_SEARCH_BUFEMPTY &&
+         m->empty_status != H264_DATA_REQUEST)) {
         ret = -EILSEQ;
         goto unlock;
     }
